Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus: Add the PLD power telemetry node

SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus: Add the PLD power telemetry node

Describe the firmware power ring at 0x81f30000 (length 0x6000, the
"pld-pep" region) as a qcom,x1e80100-pld-power device so that
qcom_pld_power binds to it. The node is in the shared romulus DTSI, so
it applies to both the 13.8 inch (romulus13) and the 15 inch
(romulus15) Surface Laptop 7.

Only the 15 inch has been validated, by the origin author (ItsLucas,
BIOS 175.235.235). The region belongs to the SoC firmware, not to the
board, which is why the 13.8 inch is expected to match, but that is
unproven; the record that said otherwise was a 15 inch booting the
romulus13 DTB. The driver fails closed: it refuses to probe unless the
range is EFI reserved memory and returns -ENODATA until the producer
counter advances. It maps the region read-only and never writes to it.
Without CONFIG_SENSORS_QCOM_PLD_POWER the node is inert.

The generic hamoa.dtsi in 7.2.8 still carries a no-map pld-pep
reservation for this range (removed upstream in 7.3, 7d240c5, because
EFI already reserves it). The two should not conflict: a no-map range is
shown as "reserved" without IORESOURCE_BUSY and is not System RAM, so
the driver's checks pass. This is read from the code, not yet seen on
hardware.

Origin: ours; node and compatible follow ItsLucas/surface-laptop-7-ubuntu-kernel (sl7_pld_device resource)
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (compatible is provisional, no upstream binding)
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
@@ -179,6 +179,18 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Firmware power telemetry ring ("pld-pep"), read-only hwmon via
+	 * qcom_pld_power. The driver only probes if EFI reports this range as
+	 * reserved memory and never writes to it. Same SoC firmware region on
+	 * the 13.8 inch (romulus13) and 15 inch (romulus15); only the 15 inch
+	 * has been validated by ItsLucas (BIOS 175.235.235).
+	 */
+	pld-power@81f30000 {
+		compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-pld-power";
+		reg = <0x0 0x81f30000 0x0 0x6000>;
+	};
+
 	reserved-memory {
 		linux,cma {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
